# Secrets - never commit
/token.txt
/REDACTED_CREDENTIALS.txt
/ftpaccess.txt
/.ftp-backups/
/schema.sql
/dblog.txt
/db-query-plan.md
/db-exports/
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.codex/settings.local.json

# OS/editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# SVN metadata (SPHERE_client/ is an SVN checkout) - pristine copies under
# .svn/ hold pre-redaction originals of files we've since redacted; never
# let these be committed even if SPHERE_client/ itself gets added later.
.svn/

# Large local-only working directories (tens of thousands of files each) -
# not meant to be committed, just tripped VS Code's Git "too many active
# changes" warning (2026-09-11):
# - old-sphere/SPHERE_client/ - SVN checkout of the decompiled Flash client
#   source (game.as, reqvestdata.as, etc.), used as a read-only reference
#   while porting; the old-sphere/ codebase proper (the archived PHP/AS
#   already checked in) remains tracked as-is.
# - client-assets/ - FFDec-decompiled building/ground sprites, a scratch
#   extraction workspace; regenerable from the source .swf files. Only the
#   final selected PNGs that make it into client/public/assets/ are tracked.
/old-sphere/SPHERE_client/
/client-assets/

# Local prototype previews and application caches
/tmp/
/технологический стек1/tmp/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.blend1
